{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1549310-mothers-of-the-firstborn","id":1549310,"title":"Mothers of the Firstborn?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-14T10:24:30-07:00","id":1549310,"title":"Mothers of the Firstborn?","content":"Do we know anything about the mothers and fathers of the Firstborn other than that Wolf laid with them? Are they still around? If they were pangeans could they have become spirits that could be contacted? Even if they are weaker than their get, couldn't they be very valuable spirits for totems and lodges that could have very interesting relationship ties to other spirits and tribes, potentially interesting dynamics with Lunes and the Firstborn, both pure and forsaken, and a decent bit of power to potentially offer.<br /> <br /> If not does anyone have any speculation on who the parents were?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-14T10:46:54-07:00","id":1549312,"title":"","content":"Afaik, everything known about them is that they're spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T22:20:10-07:00","id":1549382,"title":"","content":"I'm coming in here from primarily first edition, so I might have missed something in second. But...<br /> <br /> ...as mentioned above all we know is that they are spirits and thus you get an oppertunity for some creative work here.<br /> <br /> The only thing I've ever decided on them for myself is that they were powerful wolf spirits who mostly played ball with Father Wolf's duties I don't see them hooking up if these wolf spirits had been trouble makers on Father Wolf's radar. But beyond that, I keep it kind of open if I should come upon a really solid idea or concept that would involve them.<br /> <br /> As they don't play much of a role for the werewolves I would however assume that they had only a short fling with Father Wolf that didn't really go very far before they separated and broke off from each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T14:31:28-08:00","id":1556197,"title":"","content":"Not all of the non-Great Wolf parents had to be wolves, themselves. Consider each Firstborn has a range of concept attached to them. Father Wolf's mates could very easily have been all sorts of things!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T15:21:38-08:00","id":1556202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1549310-mothers-of-the-firstborn?p=1556197#post1556197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all of the non-Great Wolf parents had to be wolves, themselves. Consider each Firstborn has a range of concept attached to them. Father Wolf's mates could very easily have been all sorts of things!</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, The Sundered World is pretty direct:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Eras p60</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Great Predator once lay with the mightiest spirits of wolves in the Shadow, for even a Pangaean progenitor needs solace from the struggles of the hunt. It became parent to a brood of squabbling brats \u2014 the Firstborn, potent wolf-beings that serve Urfarah as heralds and messengers.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T16:15:02-08:00","id":1556204,"title":"","content":"Ah, shit. Missed that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T20:40:43-08:00","id":1556220,"title":"","content":"I think most of it comes from Lore of the Forsaken but as far as I can tell with a quick search it's just a few lines from Red Wolf, Rabid Wolf, and Silver Wolf's write-ups. Each of the Firstborn totems got a write-up there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In some legends Red Wolf is the healthy twin of Rabid Wolf, though in just as many con\ufb02icting tales, each of the Firstborn had a different mother.<br /> <br /> Each of Urfarah\u2019s Firstborn children was born to a different mother. Uratha legends say that among these female wolf-spirits, the most noble and regal mother bore in turn the most noble and regal child: Silver Wolf.<br /> <br /> Tales of Uratha history that have managed to survive through the years tell that the union that produced Gurim was a dif\ufb01cult one. The wolf-spirit mother sickened and wasted away as her Essence became tainted as if by a Wound, and her child was created from this corrupted Essence. After his birth, it soon became clear that Rabid Wolf was affected by his diseased parentage. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}